---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import BigCaseBoard from "../components/BigCaseBoard.astro";
import Stamp from "../components/Stamp.astro";
import EventKey from "../components/EventKey.astro";
---
<Base title="FedCourtsAI" description="Which Supreme Court cases matter, according to three frontier AI models — called before the Court acts, on a public, timestamped ledger." wide>
  <h1>Which Supreme Court cases matter, called before the Court acts</h1>
  <p>
    Three AI models (Claude from Anthropic, Codex from OpenAI, and Gemini from Google) read cases pending at the
    Supreme Court and predict what the Court will do. Every prediction is saved to a public record with a timestamp
    before the Court acts, so anyone can check later how the models did. <a href="/how-it-works">How it works</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    This page ranks the cases the models think matter most. Each model gives every case a <strong>big-case score</strong> from 0
    (routine) to 1 (landmark). Because the scores are recorded in advance, what counted as a big case
    can't be redefined after the term ends.
  </p>
  <p>
    <small>
      The score is an opinion, not a forecast: it isn't graded, and a high score doesn't mean the Court will take the case.
      Tap a case to see each model's reasoning and its predictions.
    </small>
  </p>
  <p><Stamp /></p>
  <EventKey />
  <BigCaseBoard />
</Base>
